 does no danage : the aquarium -- Robbery in the aquarium -- Poor fish -- Laughing at animals -- Pitying animals -- Buying animals -- The language of animals -- The taming of the shrew -- The covenant -- The perennial retainers -- Morals and weapons.","note":{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Illustrated by the author and with a foreword by Julian Huxley. [Translation from the German by Marjorie Kerr Wilson]"},"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Animal behavior"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Behavior, Animal"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QL751 .L695"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"000079168"},{"@authority":"ddc","#text":"591.5"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":[{"title":"King Solomon's ring"},{"@type":"uniform","title":"Er redete mit dem Vieh, den Vögeln und den Fischen. English"}],"name":{"namePart":"Lorenz, Konrad, 1903-1989."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York, Crowell [1952]"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)595980524"}},{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":[{"title":"King Solomon's ring"},{"@type":"uniform","title":"Er redete mit dem Vieh, den Vögeln und den Fischen. English"}],"name":{"namePart":"Lorenz, Konrad, 1903-1989."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York, Crowell [1952]"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)608579509"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990006678780203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^52007373^/L/r832"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"172314"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000460377627","#text":"Ernst Mayr Library of the Museum of Comparative Zoology, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"Z-L869"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000046073724X","#text":"Cabot Science Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QL751 .L695"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QL751 .L695"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000460710151","#text":"Tozzer Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"SOC. L 887 kE"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000460342846","#text":"Monroe C. Gutman Library, Graduate School of Education, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QL751 .L695"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Cabot Science","Gutman Education","Lamont","Museum Comp Zoology","Tozzer"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990006678780203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"000667878"}},"processingDate":"2025-05-21T05:16Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"730102"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20020606"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990006678780203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"titleInfo":{"title":"King Solomon's ring","subTitle":"new light on animal ways"},"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Lorenz, Konrad",{"@type":"date","#text":"1903-1989"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Wilson, Marjorie Kerr","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"translator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Huxley, Julian",{"@type":"date","#text":"1887-1975"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author of introduction, etc"}}}],"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London"}}],"publisher":"Methuen","dateIssued":[1952,{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1952"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xix, 202 p. illus. 22 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"Solomon, the legend goes, had a magic ring which enabled him to speak to the animals in their own language. Konrad Lorenz was gifted with a similar power of understanding the animal world. He was that rare beast, a brilliant scientist who could write (and indeed draw) beautifully. He did more than any other person to establish and popularize the study of how animals behave, receiving a Nobel Prize for his work. King Solomon's Ring, the book which brought him worldwide recognition, is a delightful treasury of observations and insights into the lives of all sorts of creatures, from jackdaws and water-shrews to dogs, cats and even wolves. Charmingly illustrated by Lorenz himself, this book is a wonderfully written introduction to the world of our furred and feathered friends, a world which often provides an uncanny resemblance to our own."},"tableOfContents":"Foreword by Julian Huxley -- Preface -- Animals as a Nuisance -- Something that Does No Damage: the Aquarium -- Robbery in the Aquarium -- Poor Fish -- Laughing at Animals -- Pitying Animals -- Buying Animals -- The Language of Animals -- The Taming of the Shrew -- The Covenant -- The Perennial Retainers -- Morals and Weapons.","note":{"@type":"statement of r